  "problem": "Monica bought $10\\,\\text{m}$ of cotton fabric and paid $$39.50.$ What is the price per meter of cotton fabric?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Expressed as a **decimal number**, a meter of cotton fabric costs $ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
  "worked_solution": "The meter of cotton fabric costs $$(39.50÷10).$\n\nTo perform this division, all we need to do is move the decimal point one place to the left:\n\n$$\n39.50\\to 3.950=3.95\n$$\n\nTherefore, $39.50÷10=3.95.$",
